From 370aac707e1419a0a12971cab357c81a5bc0ddb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Zim <info@zimcontent.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:39:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(runner): a person's input goes on the tab's own
 DevTools socket

With a person in control, each click or key went through agent-browser's
relay (POST /api/command), which runs inside the daemon behind the same
lock as its commands. The daemon holds that lock for its own upkeep too
(every 100 ms it applies what Chrome told it; each cross-origin frame
that attaches, such as a Cloudflare check, is prepared there with calls
in series that may wait 30 s). On such a page every input waited 5 s and
failed: "this didn't reach the page".

While a person drives, the runner opens the active tab's DevTools socket
(the target from the stream's tab list) and sends the input there, as the
same calls agent-browser makes (mouse, insertText, keys, chords with
their codes, the field check). The first frame of the live view in that
mode comes from there too. The relay stays the fallback when the socket
does not open. ADR 0040 section 17.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
